   b) decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate or otherwise reverse engineer Shulkaero, or attempt to
      obtain its source code, except where and only to the extent that applicable law expressly
      allows this despite this restriction;
   c) upload, mirror or distribute Shulkaero anywhere other than as part of a modpack under
      section 3, or offer it as your own work;
   d) use the textures, models, icons, sounds or texts of Shulkaero in other projects;
   e) remove or change this license or any copyright notice.

5. Compatibility development
   Shulkaero currently publishes no API of its own. You may use the official Shulkaero jar
   files as compile-only dependencies to develop, compile and distribute your own mods that
   detect or interact with Shulkaero. Your mod must not contain any part of Shulkaero; players
   install Shulkaero separately. Sections 1 and 4 apply in all other respects.

